Read-only structural reconstruction identifies the upstream contract error: `sourceFaceSheets` is a local close/opposing-sheet isolation partition, not automatically a producer-topology partition. The torus has two classifier-local disk labels whose exact source-adjacent union is one annular hard-feature region; their separating edges are non-hard classifier cuts. Treating those cuts as exterior bounded-disk rails creates the invalid corner now caught by the turn validator.

Do not relax the boundary-turn/index contract. The next correction is to distinguish:

1. **source-topological producer regions** — exact source adjacency split by genuine hard/barrier/source-boundary authority; and
2. **local isolation sheets** — retained for proximity/capture/projection safety and provenance.

A non-hard cross-sheet edge may be an internal isolation seam when exact shared-edge adjacency and reciprocal field transport prove continuity. No Euclidean or positional sheet merge is authorized.

